Architecture plan for issues #214-#216

Current module structure
- Runtime is a single Rust Axum server in `rust-backend/src/main.rs` with server-rendered Askama templates from `rust-backend/templates/`.
- Public post loading and image URL mapping live in `rust-backend/src/posts/mod.rs`; page-specific view contexts are assembled in `rust-backend/src/main.rs` and rendered by `rust-backend/src/html/public.rs` plus templates under `rust-backend/templates/public/` and `rust-backend/templates/partials/`.
- Admin post creation/editing/publishing lives in `rust-backend/src/posts/admin.rs`; admin form view-state lives in `rust-backend/src/html/admin.rs`; form markup is `rust-backend/templates/admin/post_form.html`.
- Static committed assets are served from `public/` by Axum. Ideavibes logo usage currently points at `public/images/ideavibes-wordmark.svg` for header/footer and `public/images/ideavibes-mark.svg` for fallback company-card logo.
- PostgreSQL schema keeps both `cover_image_key` and `square_cover_image_key`; runtime stores relative S3 object keys and signs/proxies them through `rust-backend/src/storage/mod.rs`.

Issue dependency map
- #214 (logo assets) is independent of the image-ratio behavior. It should update/replace committed files under `public/images/` and any tests/snapshots that assert logo markup, without changing routes or storage behavior.
- #215 (always use 16:9 cover for post cards) depends on public rendering only. The key call site is `post_card_context_from_post` in `rust-backend/src/main.rs`, which currently prefers `square_cover_image_url` and falls back to `cover_image_url`. It should use only `cover_image_url` for cards. The template already renders cards with `aspect-[16/9]`, so no card markup refactor should be needed.
- #216 (remove 1:1 cover requirement from admin publishing) is the natural follow-up to #215. Admin can continue preserving existing `square_cover_image_key` data for backward compatibility, but publishing validation and admin copy/form requirements must no longer require a square cover.

Key design decisions
- Keep the database schema backward-compatible initially: do not drop `square_cover_image_key` in these issues unless explicitly requested. Existing data can remain, but new public behavior should ignore it for post cards and publishing should not require it.
- Minimize public-card change to the view-context mapping rather than the DB query/model, because article pages and legacy API responses may still expose square-cover fields for compatibility.
- For #216, remove or relax validation in both save-time `validate_form` and dashboard publish-time `validate_publishable`; both paths currently enforce square image presence. Also update admin form text/tests so editors understand only the 16:9 cover is required.
- Preserve existing storage conventions: uploads remain S3-backed relative keys with `OBJECT_STORAGE_PREFIX` prepended in the storage wrapper. Do not introduce local file storage or public bucket URLs.
- Quality gates for implementation sessions: run `npm run backend:test`; run `npm run build` after template/CSS changes; run Playwright e2e only when admin publishing behavior is touched and environment is available.
